# /loop runner template (Claude Code)

`/loop` re-invokes a PROMPT on an interval. Skills load by prompt, not by `--skill/--role` flags.
Create one `/loop` entry per role:

```text
/loop every {{interval}}: Load the autonomous-work-loops skill and run one {{role}} tick in {{repo_path}}, following tick-mode. Reconstruct state from host + .agent-loops/. Do one unit of work and exit.
```

Roles: `implementer`, `reviewer`, `fixer`.

The external cost wall (ADR-0007): `/loop` does not impose a per-iteration OS timeout, so either
(a) wrap the underlying agent call in `timeout`/`gtimeout` if your `/loop` shells out, or
(b) rely on the tick's own state-derived budget checks plus a low `max_runtime_minutes_per_loop`
that the tick honors and the next iteration enforces. Prefer the guarded `codex.sh`
runner when a hard OS-level wall is required.

